First perform hostile technical verification. Trace the actual production code and try to disprove attacker control, reachability, the missing guard, and the claimed terminal effect. Do not carry a candidate forward merely because it is plausible.

Act as a separate hostile verifier for {{dedup_canonical_hypothesis_id}}. Reconstruct transaction/proposal/state creation -> ABCI registration -> target phase -> exact panic/divergence/resource site -> effect on consensus progress. Prove the attacker role can create every prerequisite without privileged or unsupported configuration. Inspect ante/message validation, proposal checks, SDK recovery, cache/transaction rollback, process supervisors, deterministic execution, and whether enough nodes encounter the same effect. Falsify if recovery contains it, only one optional node fails, the input cannot enter a committed/proposed block, or a mandatory guard dominates. Return supported/falsified/blocked and a local multi-node reproduction plan.

If and only if the technical verdict remains supported, immediately attempt the smallest safe deterministic reproduction in this same job. A failed or blocked reproduction must be recorded honestly; it must not erase a technically supported candidate that still needs manual validation.

For supported candidates, build the smallest authorized deterministic reproduction pinned to {{commit_sha}} using unit/integration tests, a local multi-validator network, simulator, or fuzzer. Capture the malicious transaction/proposal/state setup, panic stack or divergence evidence, nodes affected, and before/after block height or consensus progress. Repeat when practical. Do not touch public networks. Set reproduced, deterministically_proven, not_reproduced, or blocked and preserve exact evidence/artifacts.

For smart-contract candidates, use {{extra.fork_rpc_url}} and {{extra.fork_block}} when supplied. Never send transactions to a public network.

Do not apply the bounty-program eligibility decision and do not write the final finding in this step. Populate every verify_* and poc_* field. Use technical_verdict=falsified when the code contradicts the hypothesis, blocked only for a specific missing fact or unavailable environment, and supported only for a complete code-grounded path.

Apply the immutable bounty-program evidence to one independently checked candidate, then emit its progressive finding record.

